# Food and the house as chains (doc 62 phase 7): one asks what the other's eating, or gives an opinion on a dish, or
# remarks on what the season's putting on the table, or tells a trouble with the house; the other answers as they are
# (food.answer, food.opinion, food.remark, home.answer, home.advice), and the talk may close in kind (food.react,
# keeping.sorry, keeping.glad, keeping.nod). Every reply is the replier's own best rule, so one question has dozens of
# answers.
#
# What each beat remembers, so the reply suits what was said (2 minutes: only for this chain):
#   food.answer -> food.react: pair.mem.fa = good (a good feed) | plain (the usual)
#   talk.food -> food.remark: pair.mem.fm = lean (winter's thin table) | plenty (the season's bounty, a feast)
#   talk.home -> home.advice: pair.mem.hk = leak | smoke | damp | vermin | broken | wood | hens | noise | lodger | byre
#   anything -> keeping.sorry/glad/nod: pair.mem.k = want | grief | good | family | jest | weary | hopes (keeping.talk)
# food.opinion answers only opinions ("Fish is better than meat"), never news: every alternative of every rule that
# hands to it is an opinion about a food or a drink.

# ================================================================ FOOD: asking (-> food.answer)

rule e1_fd_ask_supper
when concept=talk.food pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family|spouses|apprentice
cooldown 1d
say What's for #supper#, then? | Eaten yet today? | What are you having tonight? | What's in your pot these days?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_supper_dusk
when concept=talk.food here.time=dusk|night
cooldown 1d
say Off home to your #supper#? | Smells like everyone's cooking but me. What are you having? | Is there a pot on at yours?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_cook
when concept=talk.food other.job=cook|baker|innkeeper|brewer
cooldown 2d
say What does someone who feeds the town eat, then? | Do you ever eat your own cooking, at the end of the day? | After feeding everyone else, what's your supper?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_pup
when concept=talk.food self.stage=adult|old other.stage=young
cooldown 1d
say What's for your dinner, #address#? | And what are you having for your #supper#? | What are they feeding you tonight?
then other: food.answer

rule e1_fd_ask_neighbour
when concept=talk.food pair.neighbours=yes
cooldown 2d
say What's cooking at yours tonight? I'll be sniffing at the wall anyway. | Your chimney's been going since noon. What's in the pot? | What's for #supper# next door, then?
then other: food.answer

# ================================================================ FOOD: an opinion (-> food.opinion)

rule e1_fd_claim_bread
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 1d
say Warm bread and butter. Nothing in the realm beats it. | A pie's only as good as its crust. | Stew's better the second day. Everyone knows that. | Cheese and an apple. That's a meal.
then other: food.opinion

scene e1_fd_claim_raw
when topic=food
cooldown 2d
a[stage=adult|old] : Cooked meat's all very well, but some days a wolf wants a bone with the red still on it. | I'd eat a rabbit whole if nobody was looking. | My grandfather said fire ruins good meat.
b[piety=devout] #told : The fire's a gift. Don't spit on it.
b[job=cook] #told : Then what am I for? Go and chew a sheep.
b[stage=young] #told : I ate a beetle once. Is that the same?
b[humour=merry|dry] #told : Say no more. I know a butcher with a back door.
b #plain : Hush. Somebody'll hear. | Fur and all? | Your grandfather had no teeth by fifty, I'll bet.
a@told : Only some days, mind. | I'm only half joking. | Mm. You may have something there.
a@plain : We're none of us so civilised as we look. | Fur and all. Bones too. | He had every one of them. He bit a magistrate once.

rule e1_fd_claim_fish
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say Fish is better than meat. There. I've said it. | A fresh fish fried in butter is worth any roast. | Give me a trout over a chop, every time.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_sweet
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say A meal's not done without something sweet after. | Honey cake. I could eat it every day and never tire. | Plum jam on everything. Everything.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_drink
when concept=talk.food self.stage=adult|old
cooldown 2d
say Cider's better than ale and I'll hear no argument. | A meal without ale is just eating. | Water's for washing. Supper wants a cup of something.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_pie
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say What goes in a pie? Anything. That's the beauty of a pie. | Pork pie, cold, on a step in the sun. That's happiness. | Never trust a pie with a soft bottom.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_onions
when concept=talk.food
cooldown 2d
say Everything starts with an onion. Everything good. | Turnips are nobody's favourite. Name me one wolf who loves a turnip. | Salt's the whole of cooking. The rest is waiting.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_merry
when concept=talk.food humour=merry
cooldown 2d
say If I ate how I wanted, I'd be barred from every tavern in the realm. | I've decided gravy is a drink. | My rule for food is simple. Whatever's nearest.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_old
when concept=talk.food stage=old
cooldown 2d
say Food tasted of something when I was young. | You pups don't know what a real pie is. | Bread's not what it was. Nothing's what it was, but bread especially.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_cook
when concept=talk.food job=cook
cooldown 2d
say Nobody salts enough. Nobody. | People think cooking's fire. It's patience. | Rare, they all say. Rare! One day I'll send it out still bleating.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_baker
when concept=talk.food job=baker
cooldown 2d
say Bread's a whole meal on its own. I'll not be told otherwise. | You can tell a town by its bread. | Day-old bread's for toasting, not for complaining about.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_brewer
when concept=talk.food job=brewer|innkeeper
cooldown 2d
say A good ale is food, you know. Barley. Practically bread. | Ale wants a bit of bread with it. Bread wants a lot of ale with it. | Cider's for pups and orchard folk. A grown wolf drinks ale.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_fisher
when concept=talk.food job=fisher|sailor
cooldown 2d
say Folk who won't eat fish have never had one an hour out of the water. | Salt fish and hard bread. Feed a crew on that and they'll never mutiny. | Fish heads make the best soup. Don't pull that face.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_farmer
when concept=talk.food job=farmer|herder
cooldown 2d
say Town folk think eggs come from a basket. | Grow it yourself and it tastes twice as good. | A field pea's worth ten from the market. Ten.
then other: food.opinion

## The realm's dishes, where you stand (opinions, so food.opinion fits)

rule e1_fd_claim_fens
when concept=talk.food here.region=mirebridge
cooldown 2d
say No fish like an eel. I'll argue it with anyone. | Jellied eel's the finest thing the Fens ever made. | A duck off the reed beds, roasted with sage. Nothing better.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_larkfield
when concept=talk.food here.region=larkfield
cooldown 2d
say Downs mutton's sweeter. It's the thyme in the grass. | Mutton stew with barley. Nothing better on a #cold# night. | The cheese off the downs is the best in the realm.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_southmeadow
when concept=talk.food here.region=southmeadow
cooldown 2d
say Our cider's wasted on the north. They drink it warm. | A pear off the tree, still warm from the sun. Where else would you live? | Southmeadow plums. Everyone else's are just practice.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_frosthollow
when concept=talk.food here.region=frosthollow
cooldown 2d
say Smoked mutton and black bread. Food that knows it's winter. | A miner's pasty. Eat it with your paws and your eyes shut. | Salt meat's better than fresh. It's had time to think.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_coldwater
when concept=talk.food here.region=coldwater
cooldown 2d
say Glasswater trout. The rest of the realm eats mud by comparison. | Lake char, smoked over juniper. Best thing a fish can become. | Clean water, sweet fish. That's the whole secret.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_oakhaven
when concept=talk.food here.region=oakhaven
cooldown 2d
say Mushrooms and venison. The Warmwood feeds you, if you know it. | Wild boar, slow roasted. Nothing finer. | Hazelnuts in the bread. That's how bread should be.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_claim_ridgemere
when concept=talk.food here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 2d
say Ridgemere's a fish city. Herring, mussels, crab. Who needs a field? | Best thing in this city's the chowder off the wharf. | Everything in this city tastes faintly of the sea. I like it.
then other: food.opinion

rule e1_fd_tavern
when concept=talk.food here.place=tavern
cooldown 1d
say The pie here's better than it has any right to be. | The fish here's been dead a week. You can tell. | Whatever the cook's done to that stew, it's working.
then other: food.opinion

# ================================================================ FOOD: the season, the feast (-> food.remark)

rule e1_fd_season_winter
when concept=talk.food here.season=winter
cooldown 1d
say Turnips again. I'd give a tooth for a fresh pea. | Salt pork, salt fish, salt everything. | The cellar's half empty and it's not midwinter.
then other: food.remark
remember pair: fm=lean 2m

rule e1_fd_season_spring
when concept=talk.food here.season=spring
cooldown 1d
say First greens of the year! Nettles three days running. | Lamb's on the market. Spring's here. | The hens are laying again. Eggs with everything.
then other: food.remark
remember pair: fm=plenty 2m

rule e1_fd_season_summer
when concept=talk.food here.season=summer
cooldown 1d
say Strawberries at the market. Ate them before I got home. | Lettuce and radishes from the yard. Crunchy suppers all week. | Peas, fresh from the pod. Like eating sunshine.
then other: food.remark
remember pair: fm=plenty 2m

rule e1_fd_season_autumn
when concept=talk.food here.season=autumn
cooldown 1d
say Blackberries in every hedge. My paws are purple. | Harvest supper's soon. I'm saving room. | Pig-killing time. Sausages for weeks.
then other: food.remark
remember pair: fm=plenty 2m

rule e1_fd_festival
when concept=talk.food here.day=festival
cooldown 1d
say Have you tried the roast? Go, before it's gone. | They've a whole ox turning by the well. | I've let my belt out twice. There's one hole left.
then other: food.remark
remember pair: fm=plenty 2m

rule e1_fd_restday_fast
when concept=talk.food here.day=rest piety=devout
cooldown 1d
say Not a crumb till after chapel. My belly's praying louder than I am. | I keep the Restday fast. Mostly. There was a biscuit. | Nothing till the bell. The Bright One can hear my stomach, I'm sure.
then other: keeping.nod

# ================================================================ FOOD: telling them, unasked (-> keeping.*)

rule e1_fd_tell_poor
when concept=talk.food wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 2d
say Bread and water till Marketday. | I can make one onion last three days. It's an art. | I bought the bones the butcher was throwing out. Soup for a week.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_hungry
when concept=talk.food hungry=yes
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say I've not eaten since yesterday morning. | Don't say pie. Don't say anything. | My belly's been growling at strangers.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_dole
when concept=talk.food on_dole=yes
cooldown 2d
say The parish soup's water with a rumour of leek. | Parish bread again. I'm grateful. I'm sick of it. | They gave us dole cheese. Hard as a paving stone.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_rich
when concept=talk.food wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say Our new cook's from Southmeadow. You can taste the sun in her sauces. | We had a pheasant at dinner. Nobody liked it but me. | I've a cellar of wine I'll never drink through.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_spouse
when concept=talk.food self.spouse
cooldown 2d
say #self.spouse# cooked last night. Something new. I'm still not sure what. | #self.spouse# hides the honey from me. I always find it. | #self.spouse# makes the best dumplings in town. Don't tell my mother.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_child
when concept=talk.food self.child
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# won't eat anything green. Anything. | #self.child# ate a whole loaf on the way home from the baker. | #self.child# made me breakfast. I ate it. I'm brave.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_widowed
when concept=talk.food widowed=yes
cooldown 2d
say I still cook for two. Habit. The neighbours eat well. | Nobody to cook for. I just eat bread now. | Their stew. I can't get it right. I keep trying.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_working
when concept=talk.food working=yes shift=during
cooldown 2d
say Haven't stopped for a bite since dawn. | I'll eat when it's done. If it's ever done. | Crust in my pocket. That's dinner.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=weary 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_travelling
when concept=talk.food travelling=yes
cooldown 1d
say Road food. Hard cheese and harder bread. | Every inn on the road does the same stew. The same stew! | I've eaten in nine taverns this month. One was good.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=weary 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_sump
when concept=talk.food quarter=sump
cooldown 2d
say The Soup Kitchen's doing barley this week. We queued twice. | Pickles and bread off the Sump Market. It's a supper. | A crate of cabbages fell off a cart on the wharf. We ate like lords.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fd_tell_heights
when concept=talk.food quarter=heights
cooldown 2d
say Dinners every night on the Heights this season. The whole street smells of roast. | They served snails next door. Snails! I saw the shells go out. | Everyone on the Heights has a new cook from Southmeadow. Ours too.
then other: keeping.nod

## A pie promised, between friends (the one who promised remembers it: self.mem.pie_host)

scene e1_fd_promise_pie
when topic=food pair.band=friends|family
once per other
remember pair: pie_promised 7d
remember self: pie_host 7d
a[stage=adult|old] : I'll bake you a pie this week. Hold me to it. | Come by on Restday. I'll make a stew big enough for two. | I owe you a supper. I've not forgotten.
b[warmth=cold] : If you like. | If you must. | Don't trouble yourself.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : You're a good friend. I'll not say no. | I'll bring the bread. Such as it is. | I'll not pretend I don't need it.
b[humour=merry] : I'm holding you to it in front of witnesses. | I'll come hungry. Very hungry. | I'll remind you every day till you do.
b[stage=young] : A whole pie? For me? | Is there pudding after? | Can I bring a friend?
b : I'll hold you to that. | I'll be there. | I'll believe it when I smell it.
a : Hold me, then. | Bring a big bowl. | Fair.

scene e1_fd_pie_owed_host
when topic=food pair.mem.pie_promised a.mem.pie_host
cooldown 2d
a : About that supper I promised you. I've not forgotten. | That pie I owe you. It's coming. Truly. | I keep meaning to have you round. This week. I swear it.
b[warmth=cold] : If you say so.
b[humour=merry] : I've been starving myself for it since you said.
b : I'll believe it when it's on the table. | Coming from where? The moon? | You said that last week.

scene e1_fd_pie_owed_guest
when topic=food pair.mem.pie_promised b.mem.pie_host
cooldown 2d
a : That pie you promised. I'm still waiting. | I've kept my belly free for that supper of yours. | My nose keeps turning towards your door. Something about a pie.
b : This week. I swear it. | Don't. I'm ashamed enough. | It's coming. Good pies take time.

# ================================================================ FOOD: the answer (self says what they're eating)

rule e1_fa_plain
when concept=food.answer
say Bread and whatever's in the pot. | Stew. It's always stew. | Bread and cheese, same as ever. | Whatever I can find, when I get in.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_plain2
when concept=food.answer
say Porridge, and a rasher if I'm lucky. | Soup, bread, bed. | Haven't decided. Something with onions. | Yesterday's pie, warmed up.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_poor
when concept=food.answer wealth=poor
say Turnip broth. Again. | Bread and dripping. Same as yesterday. | A heel of cheese and hope.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fa_destitute
when concept=food.answer wealth=destitute
priority 1
say Nothing yet. Maybe nothing at all. | Whatever the baker throws out at dusk. | I've a crust. That's my day.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fa_rich
when concept=food.answer wealth=rich
say Duck, I think. Or goose. Cook decides. | Venison with a plum sauce. Quite nice. | We've guests, so something grand. I'll raid the kitchen for bread after. | Eight courses. One of them a jelly with a fish in it.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e1_fa_hungry
when concept=food.answer hungry=yes
priority 2
say Nothing! Don't even ask. | I've not eaten since yesterday. | Don't talk about food. I'll cry.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fa_dole
when concept=food.answer on_dole=yes
priority 1
say The parish loaf. All of it, in one go. | Dole soup. It's soup, near enough. | Whatever the chapel's giving.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fa_homeless
when concept=food.answer homeless=yes
priority 2
say Nothing to cook on, nowhere to cook it. | Whatever I'm given. | A crust from the tavern's back door.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fa_cook
when concept=food.answer job=cook
say I cooked for thirty today. I'll eat bread and cheese standing up. | Whatever's stuck to the bottom of the pot. Best bits. | The cook's leavings. Which is to say, mine.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_baker
when concept=food.answer job=baker
say Bread. What else? Yesterday's, mind. | The loaves that came out wrong. | A bun. A big one. I earned it.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_brewer
when concept=food.answer job=brewer
say Bread and ale. It's barley twice over. | Whatever goes with the new barrel. | Tasting, mostly. It counts.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_innkeeper
when concept=food.answer job=innkeeper
say Whatever the guests didn't finish. Don't tell them. | The stew. I always eat the stew. I know what's in it. | Nothing till the last one's gone home. Then the whole pot.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_fisher
when concept=food.answer job=fisher|sailor
say Fish. Always fish. Happy with fish. | The ones too small to sell. Sweetest. | Whatever came up in the net this morning, fried.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_farmer
when concept=food.answer job=farmer
say Eggs. The hens won't stop. | Our own peas, our own pork. Can't beat it. | Whatever we didn't sell at market, which was the best of it.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_herder
when concept=food.answer job=herder
say Mutton. Not any I knew, I hope. | Curds and bread out on the hill. | Oatcakes and a bit of cheese, by the fold.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_guard
when concept=food.answer job=guard|soldier
say Watch House porridge. Thick enough to stop an arrow. | Sausage and bread, eaten on the walk. | Whatever's left when the night watch is done with it.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_miner
when concept=food.answer job=miner
say A pasty, eaten in the dark. | Something hot, if there's any left when I'm up. | Whatever's not got rock dust in it.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_woodcutter
when concept=food.answer job=woodcutter
say Enough for three. I've been swinging an axe all day. | Bread, cheese, a raw onion. Woodcutter's dinner. | Anything. Everything. Twice.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_laborer
when concept=food.answer job=laborer|carter
say Bread and a lump of bacon, sat on the cart. | A bowl of something from the cookshop. Don't ask what. | Pease pudding. It sticks to your ribs.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_servant
when concept=food.answer job=servant
say What comes back from the family's table. | The kitchen gets the ends. I like the ends. | Bread and dripping in the scullery. Standing up.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_priest
when concept=food.answer job=priest
say Whatever my flock sends round. Tonight, a pie of some sort. | Plain food. The Bright One likes plain. | A widow sent me a cake. I mustn't say it was dry.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_young
when concept=food.answer stage=young
say Porridge. I hate porridge. | Bread and jam! Mostly jam. | I don't know. Something with cabbage. I can smell it from here.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_old
when concept=food.answer stage=old
say Soft things. My teeth have retired. | Broth, and bread soaked in it. Same as every night. | Not much. You eat less, at my age.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_spouse
when concept=food.answer self.spouse
cooldown 1d
say #self.spouse#'s cooking, so something burnt. | Whatever #self.spouse# has on. I don't ask. | #self.spouse#'s famous dumplings. Famous in our house.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_fa_child
when concept=food.answer self.child
cooldown 1d
say Whatever #self.child# leaves on the plate. | #self.child# says it's soup tonight. #self.child# made it. Gods help me. | Bread. #self.child# ate everything else.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_fa_widowed
when concept=food.answer widowed=yes
say I cook for one now. Still make too much. | Bread and cheese. I can't be bothered, for one. | Their stew. I'm learning it.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e1_fa_working
when concept=food.answer working=yes shift=during
say Haven't stopped long enough to think. | Bread in my pocket. Eaten standing. | Later. If there's a later.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=weary 2m

rule e1_fa_travelling
when concept=food.answer travelling=yes
say Whatever the next inn's got. | Road cheese. It's a kind of cheese. | Hard bread and an apple, walking.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_devout_rest
when concept=food.answer piety=devout here.day=rest
say Nothing till the bell. It's Restday. | I'm keeping the fast. Ask me after chapel. | A crust and a prayer.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_fa_short
when concept=food.answer temper=short
say Why does everyone want to know what I eat? | Food. I'll be eating food. | My business.

rule e1_fa_merry
when concept=food.answer humour=merry
cooldown 1d
say Three suppers, one after the other. | Whatever's not nailed down. | A pie inside a pie. I'm working on the idea.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=jest 2m

rule e1_fa_sump
when concept=food.answer quarter=sump
say Whatever's cheap at the Sump Market. | Porridge from the stall at the bottom of our lane. | Soup Kitchen soup. Same pot as yesterday.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_fa_winter
when concept=food.answer here.season=winter
say Salt pork and the last of the turnips. | Pease pudding. It's been on since dawn. | Broth, and lots of it.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_spring
when concept=food.answer here.season=spring
say Nettle soup. It's the hungry gap. | Eggs. The hens are back at it. | The last of the cellar and the first of the greens.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_summer
when concept=food.answer here.season=summer
say Bread and cheese. Too hot to cook. | Peas, raw from the pod. | Cold mutton and a cucumber.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_autumn
when concept=food.answer here.season=autumn
say Apples with everything. | Sausages. Pig-killing week. | Blackberry and apple. The pie, I mean.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_fens
when concept=food.answer here.region=mirebridge
say Eel. What else? | Duck, if my sling was true. | Eel pie. My mother's eel pie.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_frosthollow
when concept=food.answer here.region=frosthollow
say Smoked mutton and black bread. | Oats and mutton fat. Keeps the cold out. | Whatever keeps. Which up here is everything.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_coldwater
when concept=food.answer here.region=coldwater
say Trout. Fried in butter. | Char off the boats this morning. | A fish I caught off the jetty. Proud of it.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_oakhaven
when concept=food.answer here.region=oakhaven
say Mushrooms on toast. I picked them myself. | Rabbit. Somebody's snare was generous. | Venison stew. Somebody's cousin is a hunter.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_larkfield
when concept=food.answer here.region=larkfield
say Mutton. You're in Larkfield. | Mutton pie. Larkfield's answer to everything. | Downs cheese and an apple.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

rule e1_fa_southmeadow
when concept=food.answer here.region=southmeadow
say Bread, a wedge of cheese, a peach. A cup of cider. | Plums. I'm sick of plums. Don't tell anyone. | Pork and apples. Everything here comes with apples.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=good 2m

rule e1_fa_ridgemere
when concept=food.answer here.region=ridgemere
say Herring, as ever. | Fish soup from the Sump Market. Cheap and hot. | A pie from a stall on the Commons.
then other: food.react
remember pair: fa=plain 2m

# ================================================================ FOOD: hearing what they eat (self reacts)
# fa=good: a good feed; fa=plain: the usual. Trait replies here fit both.

rule e1_fr_plain
when concept=food.react
say Mm. I'd eat that. | That'll keep you going. | Can't go wrong with that.

rule e1_fr_good
when concept=food.react pair.mem.fa=good
say Lucky you. | Listen to that. Living well. | Now I'm hungry. Thanks for that. | Save me a bit.

rule e1_fr_good2
when concept=food.react pair.mem.fa=good
say I'll be round at yours, then. | That's a proper supper. | My belly's jealous.

rule e1_fr_usual
when concept=food.react pair.mem.fa=plain
say It fills a belly. | Could be worse. | The old faithful. | Same as me, near enough.

rule e1_fr_usual2
when concept=food.react pair.mem.fa=plain
say Well, it'll keep you on your feet. | Nothing wrong with that. | Plain's honest.

rule e1_fr_hungry
when concept=food.react hungry=yes
priority 1
say Stop. My belly heard that. | I'd fight you for it. | Don't. I've not eaten.

rule e1_fr_poor
when concept=food.react wealth=poor|destitute
say Better than mine. | I'd swap you in a heartbeat. | That's a feast, where I'm sat.

rule e1_fr_rich
when concept=food.react wealth=rich pair.mem.fa=plain
say How... hearty. | I've always wondered what that tastes like. | Quite right. Simple is best. So they say.

rule e1_fr_warm
when concept=food.react warmth=warm
say Come and have yours at mine one night. | Oh, that sounds lovely. Eat it hot. | Bring it round one night and we'll share.
remember pair: pie_promised 7d
remember self: pie_host 7d

rule e1_fr_merry
when concept=food.react humour=merry
say And for afters? Another one? | I'll be round at the smell. | Put my name on a bowl.

rule e1_fr_dry
when concept=food.react humour=dry
say Living like a lord. | They'll write songs about it. | Steady, now. Don't let it go to your head.

rule e1_fr_short
when concept=food.react temper=short
say Right. | Good for you. | I didn't really want to know.

rule e1_fr_cook
when concept=food.react job=cook|baker
say I'd have done it with more salt. | Who cooked it? I want to know. | Not bad. Mine's better.

rule e1_fr_old
when concept=food.react stage=old
say We'd have called that a feast, in my day. | Mind you chew it. | That's what my mother made.

rule e1_fr_young
when concept=food.react stage=young
say Can I have some? | Is there pudding? | I'd rather have honey cake.

# ================================================================ FOOD: an opinion (self answers an opinion on food)

rule e1_fo_plain
when concept=food.opinion
say #agree#. Can't argue with that. | Depends who's cooking. | Now you've made me hungry. | You and your belly.

rule e1_fo_plain2
when concept=food.opinion
say Hm. Maybe. | I'll take your word for it. | There's worse things to think about. | Speak for yourself.

rule e1_fo_disagree
when concept=food.opinion honesty=frank
say No. Wrong. Completely wrong. | That's daft and you know it. | I've never heard such #nonsense#.

rule e1_fo_dry
when concept=food.opinion humour=dry
say Write it on your grave. | Bold stand to take. | The realm can rest easy now.

rule e1_fo_merry
when concept=food.opinion humour=merry
say Ha! You'd marry your supper if they'd let you. | I'll drink to that. I'll drink to anything. | Say it louder. The cook's listening.

rule e1_fo_short
when concept=food.opinion temper=short
say Do you ever talk about anything but your stomach? | Fine. Whatever you say. | I don't care what you eat.

rule e1_fo_warm
when concept=food.opinion warmth=warm
say Come and eat with us one night. You can prove it at my table. | You'd get on with my mother. She says the same. | I'll cook you something on Restday and you can tell me again.
remember pair: pie_promised 7d
remember self: pie_host 7d

rule e1_fo_hungry
when concept=food.opinion hungry=yes
priority 1
say Stop. Please. I've not eaten. | Can we talk about something else? Anything. | I'd agree with anything you said, if you fed me.

rule e1_fo_poor
when concept=food.opinion wealth=poor|destitute
say Some of us eat what we can get, and have no opinions about it. | Must be nice, having opinions about food. | Whatever's cheap is my favourite.

rule e1_fo_rich
when concept=food.opinion wealth=rich
say Our cook would argue with you. Our cook argues with everyone. | I leave all that to the kitchen, I'm afraid. | How refreshingly simple.

rule e1_fo_cook
when concept=food.opinion job=cook
say Spoken like someone who's never had to cook it. | Half right. The other half's the fire. | Come and say that in my kitchen.

rule e1_fo_baker
when concept=food.opinion job=baker
say Not without good bread, it isn't. | Ask a baker. We know. | All food's just a way of getting bread to your mouth.

rule e1_fo_old
when concept=food.opinion stage=old
say In my day we were grateful for anything. | Opinions! In my day you ate what was put in front of you. | I've been eating sixty years. You'll change your mind.

rule e1_fo_young
when concept=food.opinion stage=young
say Ew. | Only if there's honey on it. | Grown-ups like the strangest things.

rule e1_fo_devout
when concept=food.opinion piety=devout
say Give thanks for it, whatever it is. | The Bright One provides. Even that. | Gluttony's a sin, you know. Pass it here.

rule e1_fo_spouses
when concept=food.opinion pair.band=spouses
say You say that every night, #dear#. | You would say that. | Then you can do the cooking for once.

rule e1_fo_from_fens
when concept=food.opinion from=mirebridge
say Not compared to an eel. | You've never had a Fen supper. | Back home, we'd put eel in it.

rule e1_fo_from_south
when concept=food.opinion from=southmeadow
say Not like at home. Nothing is. | You've never had it with Southmeadow cider, then. | Back home, we'd have it with apples.

rule e1_fo_from_north
when concept=food.opinion from=frosthollow
say Up in the valley we'd smoke it. | Smoked is better. Everything's better smoked. | Wants more fat. For the cold.

rule e1_fo_from_coldwater
when concept=food.opinion from=coldwater
say It's not a patch on a Glasswater trout. | Ask a lake fisher. We'll set you right. | Fair enough. It'll float.

rule e1_fo_from_larkfield
when concept=food.opinion from=larkfield
say Better with mutton. | Can't beat a downs supper. | Have you tried it with mint?

rule e1_fo_from_oakhaven
when concept=food.opinion from=oakhaven
say Put a mushroom in it and you'd be right. | In the Warmwood we'd say the same, with a bit of boar. | Hazelnuts. It wants hazelnuts.

rule e1_fo_from_ridgemere
when concept=food.opinion from=ridgemere
say Better with a bit of fish in it. | City folk know food. Whatever they say in the towns. | Try it with a pint of Rainwater ale.

# ================================================================ FOOD: the season, the feast (self answers a remark)
# fm=lean: winter's thin table; fm=plenty: the season's bounty or a feast. Trait replies here fit both.

rule e1_fm_plain
when concept=food.remark
say That's the time of year. | Every year the same. | It comes round, doesn't it?

rule e1_fm_lean
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=lean
say Not long now. The days are drawing out. | Salt and patience. That's winter. | Roll on spring.

rule e1_fm_lean_old
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=lean stage=old
say This is nothing. The winter of the long frost, we boiled our boots. | You'll live. We always did. | Turnips kept me alive for a whole winter once. I've forgiven them.

rule e1_fm_lean_poor
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=lean wealth=poor|destitute
say Turnips! Hark at the lord. | I'd take your turnips and thank you. | We ran out of salt pork in autumn.

rule e1_fm_lean_warm
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=lean warmth=warm
say I've a jar of plums put by. Come and help me with it. | Come for supper. I'll find something that isn't salted. | I'll bring you some honey. That cheers a winter.

rule e1_fm_lean_dry
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=lean humour=dry
say Turnips build character. So people with meat tell me. | Think of it as practice for spring. | Salt everything. Including the conversation.

rule e1_fm_plenty
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=plenty
say Make the most of it. | Eat it while it's there. | Save me some. | That's the best of the year, that.

rule e1_fm_plenty_old
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=plenty stage=old
say Enjoy it. Winter's always coming. | Put some by. You'll thank me in the frost. | It's never tasted so good as when I was a pup.

rule e1_fm_plenty_poor
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=plenty wealth=poor|destitute
say Some of us only get to smell it. | If you've any going spare, I'll not say no. | Lucky you.

rule e1_fm_plenty_warm
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=plenty warmth=warm
say Bring some round. I'll bring the bread. | Oh, lovely. That's what the year's for. | Doesn't it just make you glad?

rule e1_fm_plenty_dry
when concept=food.remark pair.mem.fm=plenty humour=dry
say Enjoy it. Winter's taking notes. | Mind your belt. | Somebody's in a good mood.

rule e1_fm_hungry
when concept=food.remark hungry=yes
priority 1
say Don't. My belly's empty as a drum. | My belly heard every word of that. | I'd eat a turnip raw right now. Two.

rule e1_fm_merry
when concept=food.remark humour=merry
say Ha! My belly's been saying the same all morning. | Then let's eat. Now. Together. | I'll be at the front of that queue.

rule e1_fm_short
when concept=food.remark temper=short
say Stop moaning and eat. | Everyone's eating the same. | I don't care what's on the table.

rule e1_fm_devout
when concept=food.remark piety=devout
say Give thanks for it, either way. | The Bright One feeds us in the end. | The year turns. It always turns.

rule e1_fm_young
when concept=food.remark stage=young
say Is there cake in it anywhere? | I'm hungry now. | Mother says I eat like three.

rule e1_fm_farmer
when concept=food.remark job=farmer|herder
say That's the land for you. Feast or famine. | You eat what the year gives. | Thank a farmer while you're at it.

# ================================================================ HOME: asking (-> home.answer)

rule e1_hm_ask_house
when concept=talk.home pair.band=acquaintances|friends|apprentice|family
cooldown 1d
say How's the house? | Keeping the roof on? | All well at home? | How's your place these days?
then other: home.answer

rule e1_hm_ask_new
when concept=talk.home pair.band=strangers|acquaintances
cooldown 2d
say Are you settled, where you live? | Is it a good spot, yours? | Do you like it where you're living?
then other: home.answer

rule e1_hm_ask_weather
when concept=talk.home here.weather=rain|storm|snow
cooldown 1d
say Is your roof holding in this? | Mine's leaking like a sieve. Yours? | Dry at yours, I hope?
then other: home.answer

# ================================================================ HOME: a trouble with the house (-> home.advice)
# Only those with a home tell these. Each remembers what the trouble is (pair.mem.hk).

rule e1_hm_roof
when concept=talk.home homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The rain's found a new way in. Over the stairs, this time. | I lay awake counting drips. I got to four hundred. | The wind took the moss off my roof, and half the roof with it.
then other: home.advice
remember self: roof_leaks 3d
remember pair: hk=leak 2m

rule e1_hm_roof_still
when concept=talk.home self.mem.roof_leaks homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say Still leaking. I've a pot in every room now. | The roof again. I can hear it in my sleep. | I mended the roof. It's leaking somewhere new.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=leak 2m

rule e1_hm_chimney
when concept=talk.home homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The chimney's drawing backwards. Smoke comes down, not up. | My eyes have been streaming for a week. It's the chimney. | Every time the wind's in the west, my kitchen fills with smoke.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=smoke 2m

rule e1_hm_damp
when concept=talk.home homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say Damp's coming up the walls again. | Everything I own smells of mould. | There's a green patch on the ceiling. It's growing.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=damp 2m

rule e1_hm_mice
when concept=talk.home homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say Rats in the cellar. Big as cats. | Something's been at the bread in the night. Little teeth marks. | There's a nest behind the dresser. I can hear them squeaking.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=vermin 2m

rule e1_hm_door
when concept=talk.home homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say My shutter's off its hinge. It bangs all night. | The step's cracked right through. I go in sideways. | The floorboard by the hearth's gone soft. I put a foot through it.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=broken 2m

rule e1_hm_furniture
when concept=talk.home homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say A chair's lost a leg. Nobody's owned up to it. | My bed broke. In the night. With me in it. | The table wobbles. Soup everywhere.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=broken 2m

rule e1_hm_wood
when concept=talk.home homeless=no here.season=autumn|winter
cooldown 2d
say The woodpile's half what it should be. | Every log I've got is green. It hisses at me. | Firewood's dear this year. I'm rationing logs.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=wood 2m

rule e1_hm_hens
when concept=talk.home homeless=no here.region!=ridgemere
cooldown 3d
say My hens have taken to laying in the hedge. I'm hunting eggs like a pup. | The cockerel starts before dawn. The whole street hates me. | The goat got in with the hens again. Nobody's happy.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=hens 2m

rule e1_hm_noise
when concept=talk.home homeless=no pair.neighbours=no
cooldown 2d
say There's a baby next door that never sleeps. Nor do I, now. | The smith down the lane starts hammering before dawn. | Somebody on my street keeps geese. Have you heard geese at night?
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=noise 2m

rule e1_hm_lodger
when concept=talk.home homeless=no wealth=comfortable
cooldown 3d
say My lodger's not paid in a month. | The lodger's started cooking fish in his room. | My lodger sings in the bath. Every night. The same song.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=lodger 2m

rule e1_hm_moving
when concept=talk.home drive=restless|ambitious
cooldown 3d
say I'm thinking of leaving this town. Going anywhere. | I've seen a house I want. I can't afford it. Yet. | This street's too small for me.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=hopes 2m

# ================================================================ HOME: telling, unasked (-> keeping.*)

rule e1_hm_tell_rent
when concept=talk.home wealth=poor|destitute homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say I've counted the rent three times. It's still short. | The collector knocks the same knock every week. I hear it in my sleep. | Rent's eaten my #wages# again. There's nothing left for firewood.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_owes
when concept=talk.home owes=yes homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The landlord's man was at the door again. | I've not paid the rent. I go in by the back. | If they put me out, I don't know where I'll go.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_homeless
when concept=talk.home homeless=yes
cooldown 1d
priority 2
say I've nowhere, #address#. Not a room. | Doorways and haylofts. That's my home now. | I used to have a door I could shut.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_rich
when concept=talk.home wealth=rich homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say We're having a new wing built. The noise! | I've bought the house next door. For the garden. | New glass in every window. You should see it shine.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_heights
when concept=talk.home quarter=heights homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The Heights are all scaffolding this season. Everyone's building. | Our neighbours have a new carriage house. Ours is older. | There's a new gardener next door. He's moved every rosebush in the street.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_sump
when concept=talk.home quarter=sump homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The landlord's split our room in two with a curtain. Now there's two rents. | There's a crack in our wall you can put your arm through. | Our stair's lost a step. Nobody'll say who took it.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_wharf
when concept=talk.home quarter=wharf|docks homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The Customs men tramp past my window at all hours. | I can hear the ropes creak on the piers all night. Like a cradle. | Sailors in the room below. They sing till the tide turns.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_works
when concept=talk.home quarter=works homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say The foundry bell rings the shifts right through my sleep. | The glassworks lights my window red all night. | My lodging's over the tannery. I'll say no more.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_spouse
when concept=talk.home self.spouse homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say #self.spouse# wants a bigger house. Wants. | #self.spouse# put up a shelf. It's on the floor now. | #self.spouse# has hung herbs from every beam. I walk about ducking.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_child
when concept=talk.home self.child homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say #self.child# swept the whole floor without being asked. I nearly fainted. | #self.child# has dug a hole in the yard. A big one. Why? | #self.child# has filled the yard with snails. Pets, apparently.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_widowed
when concept=talk.home widowed=yes homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say I don't like going home in the evenings. | I still set out two cups. Every morning. | I've not moved their boots from the door. I can't.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_old
when concept=talk.home stage=old homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say Every board in my house has a voice. I know them all. | Fifty years in my house. Everything's where I can reach it. Don't move a thing. | I found a letter under the floorboards from before I was born. The house keeps secrets.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_young
when concept=talk.home stage=young homeless=no
cooldown 2d
say There's a loose board under my bed. I keep my treasures there. | I found a bird's nest in our gutter. Three eggs! | I'm allowed to bank the fire now. On my own.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_servant
when concept=talk.home job=servant
cooldown 2d
say Scrubbed their floors all day. Mine can wait. | The family count the candles. Every night. | I polish silver I'll never eat off.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=weary 2m

rule e1_hm_tell_winter
when concept=talk.home here.season=winter homeless=no
cooldown 1d
say I've hung a blanket over the door. It helps. A bit. | The wind finds every crack in my walls. I'm learning where they all are. | I keep the fire in day and night. The woodpile's weeping.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_spring
when concept=talk.home here.season=spring homeless=no
cooldown 1d
say Shutters open at last. The house can breathe. | Swallows are back in my eaves. Same pair as last year, I'm sure. | I've scrubbed the step till it shines. First time since autumn.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_summer
when concept=talk.home here.season=summer homeless=no
cooldown 1d
say Shutters shut all day, or we cook. | The thatch is full of buzzing. Something's nesting. | I sleep with the door open now. The cat comes and goes.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hm_tell_autumn
when concept=talk.home here.season=autumn homeless=no
cooldown 1d
say Woodpile's stacked to the eaves. Winter can come. | Apples drying on every shelf in the house. | I've stuffed every crack with moss and rags. Let the wind try.
then other: keeping.glad

# ================================================================ HOME: the answer (self answers about their house)

rule e1_ha_plain
when concept=home.answer
say Standing, which is all you can ask. | Much the same. Roof on, door shut. | Can't complain. Well. The damp. | It's home. It'll do.

rule e1_ha_plain2
when concept=home.answer
say Warm, dry, mostly. | Small, but mine. | There's always something. This week it's the step.

rule e1_ha_poor
when concept=home.answer wealth=poor
say Roof leaks and the rent's up. | One room, one window. It does. | I'd be fine if the landlord fell down a well. I'm joking. Mostly.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_ha_destitute
when concept=home.answer wealth=destitute
priority 1
say I'll be out by Marketday if I can't pay. | Sold the table. Sold the chairs. Still short. | Don't ask. Please.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_ha_homeless
when concept=home.answer homeless=yes
priority 3
say I've no house, #address#. | Under the bridge, tonight. | Wherever's dry.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_ha_owes
when concept=home.answer owes=yes
priority 1
say Behind on the rent. Don't tell anyone. | I go in by the back door now. Collector. | It's a roof. For now.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_ha_rich
when concept=home.answer wealth=rich
say Very well. We've had the hall done. | Splendid. The new gardens are coming on. | Too big, honestly. I lose the servants.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e1_ha_heights
when concept=home.answer quarter=heights
say Lovely view. Dreadful neighbours. | Quiet up here. You can hear the fountains. | All those steps up from the Commons. Worth it, mostly.

rule e1_ha_sump
when concept=home.answer quarter=sump
say Damp. It's the Sump. | The water's in the cellar again. And the rats. | Loud. Somebody's always fighting on our lane.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_ha_harbour_hill
when concept=home.answer quarter=harbour_hill
say My knees hate it. My eyes love it. | Steep. Everything's steep. | Up among the gulls. I like it.

rule e1_ha_wharf
when concept=home.answer quarter=wharf|docks
say Noisy. The carts start before dawn. | Handy for work. I roll out of bed onto the pier. | Salty. Everything's salty.

rule e1_ha_works
when concept=home.answer quarter=works
say Loud. The ironworks never stops. | Grey. Everything's grey. | Fine, if you don't breathe much.

rule e1_ha_commons
when concept=home.answer quarter=commons|suburbs|office
say Quiet street, nobody bothers me. Can't ask more. | Neighbours are decent. That's half of it. | The baker's two doors down. I wake to the smell of bread.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=good 2m

rule e1_ha_spouse
when concept=home.answer self.spouse
cooldown 1d
say #self.spouse# wants it painted. I want my supper. | Fine. #self.spouse# keeps it nice. I keep out of the way. | Crowded. #self.spouse# never throws anything away.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_ha_child
when concept=home.answer self.child
cooldown 1d
say #self.child# has drawn on every wall I own. | Loud. #self.child# has found a drum. | Full of #self.child#'s things. I live in the corner.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=family 2m

rule e1_ha_widowed
when concept=home.answer widowed=yes
say Too big, now. | Tidy. Nobody to make a mess. | I sleep in the chair by the fire. The bed's too wide.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=grief 2m

rule e1_ha_old
when concept=home.answer stage=old
say Draughty. Like me. | Same house fifty years. Same creaks. | My bones and the walls, both settling.

rule e1_ha_young
when concept=home.answer stage=young
say I've got the bed by the window now. | Loud. Everyone shouts at once. | There's a spider in the corner. I've named him Gorse.

rule e1_ha_crafter
when concept=home.answer job=crafter|smith
say I mend everyone's house but mine. | Fine. I fixed the roof myself. With help from gravity. | Every chair in it's my own work. None of them match.

rule e1_ha_innkeeper
when concept=home.answer job=innkeeper
say Full of strangers, as ever. | A guest snores through my wall. A different one every night. | Home's the inn. I've not had a day off it in years.

rule e1_ha_servant
when concept=home.answer job=servant
say I live in someone else's house. I've a corner of the attic. | Theirs is lovely. Mine's a cot. | Spotless. Not mine, mind.
then other: keeping.sorry
remember pair: k=want 2m

rule e1_ha_farmer
when concept=home.answer job=farmer|herder
say The house is fine. The byre's falling down. | The house is well. The barn roof's another matter. | The byre's leaning. The cows don't seem to mind.
then other: home.advice
remember pair: hk=byre 2m

rule e1_ha_priest
when concept=home.answer job=priest
say The manse is cold as charity. | I've a room behind the chapel. It suits me. | Full of other people's troubles.

rule e1_ha_restless
when concept=home.answer drive=restless
say I'd move tomorrow, if I had somewhere to go. | Same four walls. Same four walls. | Fine. Dull. I'll not be there for ever.
then other: keeping.nod
remember pair: k=hopes 2m

rule e1_ha_cold
when concept=home.answer warmth=cold
say It's a house. Walls, roof. | Fine. | Why?

rule e1_ha_merry
when concept=home.answer humour=merry
cooldown 1d
say Still standing! Mostly by habit. | It's a palace. A small, damp, leaning palace. | The roof leaks, but only on the landlord's side.
then other: keeping.glad
remember pair: k=jest 2m

rule e1_ha_winter
when concept=home.answer here.season=winter
say Cold. I can't keep the fire in. | Snug, if you sit in the hearth. | Draughty. I've a blanket over every door.

rule e1_ha_summer
when concept=home.answer here.season=summer here.weather!=rain|storm
say Close. Can't sleep for the heat. | Cool enough with the shutters closed. | The thatch keeps it cool. Mostly.

rule e1_ha_fens
when concept=home.answer here.region=mirebridge
say Damp to the rafters. Fen house. | Leaning a little more each year. Like me. | The frogs sing under the floor all spring.

rule e1_ha_frosthollow
when concept=home.answer here.region=frosthollow
say Thick walls. Thick as a mountain. | Warm, if you keep the door shut. | Peat on the fire and the shutters barred. Snug.

rule e1_ha_coldwater
when concept=home.answer here.region=coldwater
say Damp, but you can see Glasswater. | The boat's pulled up by my door. Handy. | Smells of fish and woodsmoke. I like it.

rule e1_ha_oakhaven
when concept=home.answer here.region=oakhaven
say Snug under the trees. | Green light through the windows all summer. | Built of oak by my grandfather. Not a nail in it.

rule e1_ha_larkfield
when concept=home.answer here.region=larkfield
say Old walls, thick and dry. Can't fault it. | Chalk walls. White as a fleece. | Windy. It's always windy up on the downs.

rule e1_ha_southmeadow
when concept=home.answer here.region=southmeadow
say Roses over the door. Bees in the roses. | Warm. It's always warm. | Smells of apples. It always smells of apples.

rule e1_ha_ridgemere
when concept=home.answer here.region=ridgemere
say Damp. It's Ridgemere. | The rain comes in sideways under the door. | Everything I own smells of the sea.

# ================================================================ HOME: advice (self answers a trouble with the house)
# Unkeyed replies fit any trouble (a leak, a smoking chimney, mice, a broken chair, noisy neighbours, a lodger, a
# byre, hens). Keyed ones (pair.mem.hk) answer one kind.

rule e1_hv_plain
when concept=home.advice
say That's houses for you. | There's always something, isn't there? | Mine's no better, if it helps. | What a bother.

rule e1_hv_plain2
when concept=home.advice
say Ugh. I'm sorry. | Somebody ought to see to that. | That'd drive me spare.

rule e1_hv_leak
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=leak
say Put a pot under it and pray. | Tar and a flat stone. That's what my father did. | It's never where it drips. It's always two feet over.

rule e1_hv_smoke
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=smoke
say Get the sweep in. Or a pup with a brush. | Seasoned wood, and a bit of luck. | Open a window and wear your coat.

rule e1_hv_wood
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=wood
say The woodcutters sell their offcuts cheap, if you ask nicely. | Stack it under cover and let it dry. Next year you'll thank me. | Wear your coat indoors and save the logs for the evenings.

rule e1_hv_damp
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=damp
say Lime-wash it. Every spring. | Keep the fire in all day and the damp gives up. | Rainward damp. It never really leaves.

rule e1_hv_vermin
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=vermin
say Get a cat. Cats fix everything. | Peppermint in the gaps. They hate it. | Tin over the holes. They chew through anything else.

rule e1_hv_broken
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=broken
say Get a joiner round. It's a morning's work. | Plane it down and wedge it. Done. | Have you tried hitting it?

rule e1_hv_hens
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=hens
say Hens. More trouble than eggs, some days. | Shut them in at dusk and out at dawn. They learn. | Make a pie of the worst one. The rest'll behave.

rule e1_hv_noise
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=noise
say Stuff your ears with wool. It's what I do. | You get used to it. Or you go mad. One or the other. | Sleep in the day, then. Ha. No.

rule e1_hv_lodger
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=lodger
say Turn him out. Plenty more want a room. | A lodger's a lodger. You take the rent and the rest. | Talk to him. Firmly. With the door open.

rule e1_hv_byre
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.hk=byre
say Prop it before the winter, or you'll be calving in the kitchen. | Get the neighbours in for a day. Feed them. It'll be up by dusk. | A byre's more house than the house, on a farm.

rule e1_hv_crafter
when concept=home.advice job=crafter|smith pair.mem.hk=leak|smoke|broken|damp|byre
say I'll come and look at it. Bring me a pie. | An hour with the right tool. I'll lend you the tool. | Don't touch it. You'll make it worse. I'll come round.
remember pair: offered_help 7d
remember self: helper 7d

rule e1_hv_laborer
when concept=home.advice job=laborer|woodcutter pair.mem.hk=leak|broken|wood|byre
say Give me a ladder and a morning. | I'll do it for a penny and a cup of ale. | I've a strong back and a free Restday.
remember pair: offered_help 7d
remember self: helper 7d

rule e1_hv_neighbour
when concept=home.advice pair.neighbours=yes
say Knock on my wall if you need a paw. | I'll come round after supper and see. | Borrow what you need from mine. Bring it back, mind.
remember pair: offered_help 7d
remember self: helper 7d

rule e1_hv_old
when concept=home.advice stage=old
say Houses are like knees. Something's always going. | There's always something. Sixty years I've had something. | I've had that. Twice. You live through it.

rule e1_hv_young
when concept=home.advice stage=young
say Can I help? I'm good at helping. | I'd hide under the blanket. | Is it scary?

rule e1_hv_rich
when concept=home.advice wealth=rich
say I'd pay somebody to worry about it, if I were you. | Dear me. How tiresome. | That's what one keeps a steward for.
then other: keeping.nod

rule e1_hv_poor
when concept=home.advice wealth=poor|destitute
say Live with it, like the rest of us. | At least you've a house to complain about. | I'd swap you.

rule e1_hv_warm
when concept=home.advice warmth=warm
say Oh, you poor thing. What can I do? | I'll come over on Restday and lend a paw. Don't argue. | Come round tonight and forget it for an evening.
remember pair: offered_help 7d
remember self: helper 7d

rule e1_hv_cold
when concept=home.advice warmth=cold
say Not my house. | See to it, then. | Everyone's got something.

rule e1_hv_merry
when concept=home.advice humour=merry
say Ha! Your house has it in for you. | Have you tried shouting at it? Works on my brother. | Sell tickets. Folk'd pay to see that.

rule e1_hv_dry
when concept=home.advice humour=dry
say Ah, the joys of a roof of your own. | Character, that's called. | Could be worse. Could be mine.

rule e1_hv_short
when concept=home.advice temper=short
say Well, stop telling me and see to it. | Everyone's got troubles. | And what am I to do about it?

rule e1_hv_devout
when concept=home.advice piety=devout
say Have the priest bless the threshold. It helps more than you'd think. | Pray on it. Then see to it. | The Bright One tests us in small ways too.

rule e1_hv_healer
when concept=home.advice job=healer pair.mem.hk=damp|smoke|leak
say Damp in the house is damp in the chest. Fix it before winter. | Burn rosemary. It clears the air. | Keep the fire up and the window cracked.

rule e1_hv_help_again
when concept=home.advice pair.mem.offered_help self.mem.helper
priority 1
cooldown 1d
say I said I'd come round. I meant it. | Still waiting for you to ask. | The offer stands. Name the day.
